.he "mt (1)                       8/16/26                       mt (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
mt
- print the raw mtime words of a file
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
mt file
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Mt stats the named file and prints the two sixteen-bit words that make
up its modification time, in the order they sit in memory.  The kernel
stores the time as a pair of words, and the order they come back in
shows whether a program that reads them is getting them right.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
This is a diagnostic written for the port, not the magnetic tape
manipulator the name meant on the BSD system.  It takes a file name,
not a tape command.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
ls (1)
